    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25qF7x2G9cZsuh9zB5xuSH4)_\n\n## What\n\nThe \"Changes by pull request\" sections are in the module docs (and `README.org`, a few architecture docs), not in the CHANGELOGs. In 50 `.org` files, 147 entries went from one long paragraph to:\n\n- a bullet with the PR link, and\n- one nested bullet per change (one per sentence), and a third level where a sentence had top-level `;` clauses.\n\n## Checks\n\n- Wording is unchanged: a script compared each file before and after with whitespace, `;`, `.` and `-` removed, and all files match.\n- Splits happen only outside `(...)`, `=verbatim=`, `~code~` and links. The split-out `;` is dropped and the last clause keeps its full stop.\n- Feature-set order in the CHANGELOGs is untouched. This PR edits no CHANGELOG (the rule is for future entries).\n\n## Not in this PR\n\nThe nightly tidy prompt and the `dotfiles-changelog` skill live outside the repo; they need the same rule (Sia is told in the thread).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDN6TS4cU5kG59gdQx)_",
